<%# Student Portal > Pets (routes/student-portal.js, utils/pets.js) - the
    pet illustrations themselves, kept separate from partials/icon-sprite
    (that one's plain line icons for chrome/nav; these are small creature
    illustrations meant to be composited together).
    Every body symbol shares the same 0 0 120 120 canvas with the head
    centered around (60, 44-46) so the ears/eyes/mouth/accessory overlay
    symbols line up on top of any species without per-species positioning
    - views/student-pets.ejs stacks body + ears + eyes + mouth + accessory
    as sibling <use> elements inside one <svg>. Body shapes use
    fill="currentColor" for their main coat/shell/scale color so
    utils/pets.js's per-species color options work by just setting the
    wrapping element's CSS `color`; a few fixed-color accent shapes
    (belly patches, cheeks) stay literal hex since those don't change
    with the coat color trait. Ears is its own real trait (a real
    request: "the pets, features and buttons should look exactly like my
    examples," whose reference shows Body/Ears/Eyes/Mouth/Accessories as
    five separate cyclable rows) - mammal species below draw their body
    earless and pick up whichever ears trait is selected; the reptile/
    bird species (dragon/turtle/chicken/lizard) keep their own natural
    head feature (spikes/shell dome/comb/brow ridges) as part of Body
    instead, same as a real dragon/turtle/chicken/lizard has no mammal-
    style ears to swap - their own Ears trait is a genuine no-op (see
    pet-ears-none) rather than something faked.

    "higher level graphics and glossy like my original screenshots" -
    the reference is a photorealistic 3D render (soft fur shading, rim
    light, multi-highlight sparkly eyes) that isn't achievable as
    hand-authored SVG; this pushes the flat-vector "2D game asset" style
    as close to that glossy read as the medium allows: every major mass
    (body/head/shell) gets a dark ink outline, a soft sheen/shadow
    gradient pair (#pet-sheen/#pet-shadow-edge, objectBoundingBox so they
    auto-fit any shape with no per-species tuning), AND a small opaque
    "shine" ellipse (a tighter, brighter specular glint, the kind a
    glossy render/vinyl toy has) near the upper-left of the head. Two
    small paw ovals sit under each mammal body so it reads as a sitting
    creature rather than a floating head, matching the reference's pose.
    Eyes are now a big glossy sclera + a per-species iris color (driven
    by a --eye-color CSS var - see utils/pets.js's SPECIES.eyeColor and
    student-pets.ejs/student-pets-customize.ejs's own inline style/JS)
    with a radial highlight and two graduated shine dots, instead of
    plain dark circles. %>
